Optional Linux Wayland capture dependencies:
- ashpd 0.10.2: MIT, xdg-desktop-portal ScreenCast client.
  https://github.com/bilelmoussaoui/ashpd
- pipewire-rs 0.8.0 (pipewire, pipewire-sys, libspa, libspa-sys): MIT,
  native PipeWire/SPA bindings. API usage follows upstream stream examples.
  https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/pipewire/pipewire-rs
- System PipeWire/SPA libraries: MIT, linked only with the pipewire feature.
  https://pipewire.org
These permissive licenses are compatible with this repository's Apache-2.0
license. No cargo-deny policy file is currently present in this repository.
The resolved transitive license expressions were also reviewed: MIT,
Apache-2.0 (including LLVM-exception), BSD-2/3-Clause, ISC, and Unicode-3.0
have compatible permissive terms. For multi-license expressions, a permissive
MIT/Apache option is selected (no LGPL option is required).
Transitive Rust dependencies and their exact versions are recorded in Cargo.lock.

